{
  "schema_version": "fabric.id-key-file-vectors/v1",
  "rule": "Spec 056 §7.3.3 (b) hostrecords.ReadIDKeyFile: the id key is the file's bytes exactly, the key FABRIC_WIRE_ID_KEY holds and Python's _sequence.id_key_from_env uses as its UTF-8 bytes; no hex or base64 decoding, no trimming. The file is a regular file of mode 0400 or 0440 holding 16 to 4096 bytes of UTF-8 without NUL and without a final \\n or \\r (deployments write it with printf %s, and the same Secret feeds the agents' environment). Refusals, checked in this order: mode, too_short, too_long, trailing_newline, nul_byte, not_utf8; an error never includes the file's contents. For an accepted key: host_id is the hst- v2 pseudonym of the host label 'ar1-host' and source_id the s- label pseudonym of 'node-a/ebpf' under it, and id_key_from_env({'FABRIC_WIRE_ID_KEY': the file's text}) gives the same key bytes, so an agent and a sensor fed by one Secret key every id alike.",
  "reasons": [
    "mode",
    "too_short",
    "too_long",
    "trailing_newline",
    "nul_byte",
    "not_utf8"
  ],
